The '''Argentina national football team''',{{efn|group=upper-alpha|{{langx|es|Selección de fútbol de Argentina}}}} nicknamed '''''la Albiceleste''''',&hairsp;{{efn|group=upper-alpha|English: ''The White and Sky Blue''}} represents [[Argentina]] in men's international [[Association football|football]] and is administered by the [[Argentine Football Association]], the governing body of [[football in Argentina]]. It has been a member of [[FIFA]] since 1912 and was a founding member of [[CONMEBOL]] in 1916. It was also a member of [[Panamerican Championship#Panamerican Football Confederation|PFC]], the unified confederation of the Americas, from 1946 to 1961. Argentina has won three [[FIFA World Cup]]s, in [[1978 FIFA World Cup final|1978]], [[1986 FIFA World Cup final|1986]] and [[2022 FIFA World Cup|2022]]. The team has appeared in seven World Cup [[List of FIFA World Cup finals|finals]], including the inaugural one in [[1930 FIFA World Cup final|1930]].

Argentina has won the [[Copa América]] a record 16 times, most recently in [[2024 Copa América|2024]]. With victories in [[1945 South American Championship|1945]], [[1946 South American Championship|1946]] and [[1947 South American Championship|1947]], it is the only nation to have won the tournament three consecutive times. Argentina won the [[Panamerican Championship]] in [[1960 Panamerican Championship|1960]], the [[1992 King Fahd Cup|inaugural FIFA Confederations Cup]] in 1992, and the [[CONMEBOL–UEFA Cup of Champions]] in [[1993 Artemio Franchi Cup|1993]] and [[2022 Finalissima|2022]]. Argentina holds the record for most official international titles, with 23.{{efn|group=upper-alpha|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite web |date=14 July 2024 |title=Tras la conquista de Argentina en la Copa América, así quedó la tabla histórica de títulos de las selecciones del mundo |url=https://www.infobae.com/deportes/2024/07/14/asi-esta-la-tabla-historica-de-las-selecciones-con-mas-titulos-en-el-mundo-en-la-previa-a-las-finales-de-la-copa-america-y-la-eurocopa/ |access-date=12 August 2024 |website=infobae |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Ritchie |first=Calum |date=1 June 2024 |title=The 10 most successful nations in football history ranked by major trophies won |url=https://www.givemesport.com/most-successful-nations-in-football-history-by-major-trophies-won/ |access-date=12 August 2024 |website=GiveMeSport}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Top five nations with most major international football trophies |url=https://khelnow.com/football/2023-08-world-football-most-international-football-trophies |access-date=12 August 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260713202949/https://khelnow.com/football/2023-08-world-football-most-international-football-trophies |archive-date=13 July 2026 |website=Khel Now}}</ref>}} Argentina players have won the [[FIFA World Cup awards#Golden Ball|FIFA World Cup Golden Ball]] three times: [[Diego Maradona]] in 1986, and [[Lionel Messi]] in [[2014 FIFA World Cup|2014]] and 2022. Messi has the most appearances for the team (208) and has scored the most goals (126). As of 20 July 2026,<ref>{{Cite web |title=FIFA/Coca-Cola Men's World Ranking |url=https://inside.fifa.com/fifa-world-ranking/men?dateId=FRS_Male_Football_20260611 |access-date=2026-07-20 |website=inside.fifa.com |language=en}}</ref> Argentina ranks second in the [[FIFA Men's World Ranking]]. Argentina is known for having rivalries [[Argentina–Brazil football rivalry|with Brazil]], [[Argentina–England football rivalry|England]], [[Germany national football team|Germany]], [[Argentina–Netherlands football rivalry|Netherlands]], and [[Argentina–Uruguay football rivalry|Uruguay]].

