The '''{{Lang|fr|Cinémathèque française|italic=no}}''' ({{IPA|fr|sinematɛk fʁɑ̃sɛːz}}; French [[cinematheque]]), founded in 1936, is a French non-profit film organization that holds one of the largest archives of film documents and film-related objects in the world. Based in Paris' [[12th arrondissement of Paris|12th arrondissement]], the archive offers daily screenings of films from around the world. It is the second oldest cinematheque in France, after [[Cinematheque de Saint-Etienne|Cinematheque de Saint-Etienne]], which was founded in 1922.

