The '''Germany men's national basketball team''' ({{langx|de|Deutsche Basketballnationalmannschaft}} or ''Die Mannschaft'') represents [[Germany]] in international [[basketball]] competition. The team is directed by the [[German Basketball Federation]] (''Deutscher Basketball Bund''), the governing body for [[basketball in Germany]]. Currently, Germany is ranked second in the [[FIBA Men's World Ranking|FIBA World Ranking]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fiba.basketball/en/ranking/men|title=FIBA World Ranking Presented by NIKE – Men|website=fiba.basketball}}</ref>

Between 1949 and 1990, separate German national teams were recognised by [[FIBA]] due to [[Allied-occupied Germany|Allied occupation]]. The DBB were representing the [[West Germany|Federal Republic of Germany]] (named West Germany from 1949 to 1990), while the [[East Germany men's national basketball team|East Germany team]] represented the [[East Germany|German Democratic Republic]] (1952–1990). The two would later merge, after [[German reunification|reunification]] in 1990.

Germany's greatest achievements to date have been competing in 26 appearances at the [[EuroBasket]], winning gold in [[EuroBasket 1993|1993]] and [[EuroBasket 2025|2025]], silver in [[EuroBasket 2005|2005]], and bronze in [[EuroBasket 2022|2022]]. Germany have made seven appearances at the [[FIBA Basketball World Cup|FIBA World Cup]], winning gold in [[2023 FIBA Basketball World Cup|2023]], and bronze in [[2002 FIBA World Championship|2002]]. At the [[Basketball at the Summer Olympics|Olympic Games]], in Germany's seven appearances, their top performance is their fourth place finish in [[Basketball at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2024]].

