The '''Homeland Union – Lithuanian Christian Democrats''' ({{langx|lt|Tėvynės sąjunga {{ndash}} Lietuvos krikščionys demokratai}}, '''TS–LKD'''), also colloquially known as the '''Conservatives''' ({{langx|lt|Konservatoriai|links=no}}), is a [[centre-right politics|centre-right]]<ref name="Sužiedėlis"/><ref name=Duvold-Jurkynas/><ref name=Day-East-Thomas/> [[List of political parties in Lithuania|political party]] in Lithuania. It has 18,000 members and 28 of 141 seats in the [[Seimas]]. Its current  leader is [[Laurynas Kasčiūnas]] following the resignation of [[Gabrielius Landsbergis]] in 2024 after the party's loss in the [[2024 Lithuanian parliamentary election|recent election]]. It is a member of the [[European People's Party]] (EPP).

Since 1996, the party has included the [[western house martin]] in its various [[logo]]s over the years.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://web1.mab.lt/2020-01/portfolio/vii-seimas/|title=VII Seimas &#124; Parlamentarizmas – demokratijos pagrindas|first=U. F. O.|last=Themes}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.delfi.lt/archive/partiju-simbolika-akims-pritraukti-ir-ziniai-perduoti.d?id=17959718|title=Partijų simbolika – akims pritraukti ir žiniai perduoti|website=DELFI}}</ref>

