'''Kering S.A.''' ({{IPA|fr|keʁiŋ|lang}}) is a French [[multinational corporation|multinational]] [[holding company]] specializing in [[luxury goods]]. Headquartered in [[Paris]], it owns the brands [[Gucci]], [[Yves Saint Laurent (fashion house)|Yves Saint Laurent]], [[Balenciaga]], [[Bottega Veneta]], [[Alexander McQueen (fashion house)|Alexander McQueen]], [[Creed (perfume)|Creed]], and [[Maui Jim]], among others.

The timber-trading company Pinault S.A. was founded in 1962 by [[François Pinault]]. After the company was quoted on [[Euronext Paris]] in 1988, it became the retail conglomerate Pinault-Printemps-Redoute (PPR) in 1994. The luxury group was rebranded Kering in 2013. It has been a constituent of the [[CAC 40]] since 1995. [[François-Henri Pinault]] has been President of Kering since 2005, and [[Luca de Meo]] CEO since September 2025.

