<!-----Needs [[WP:LEADFOLLOWSBODY]] ----->

'''OpenAI''' is an American [[artificial intelligence]] (AI) [[Benefit corporation|public benefit corporation]] (PBC) headquartered in [[San Francisco]], California.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-09-14 |title=Tech leaders, governments split over 'AI doom' fears |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/what-amodei-altman-musk-have-said-about-ai-risks-stoking-doom-fears-2026-10-14/ |access-date=2026-10-15 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref> It develops [[Foundation model#Frontier models|"frontier"]] [[generative AI]] models, particularly its [[Products and applications of OpenAI#Text generation|generative pre-trained transformer (GPT) series]] of [[large language model]]s.

Its release of [[ChatGPT]] in November 2022 accelerated an [[AI boom]], leading to widespread use of generative AI; {{As of|2026|Sep|lc=y}}, ChatGPT is the [[List of most-visited websites|fifth-most-visited website]] globally.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Most Visited Websites in Worldwide 2025 {{!}} Trending Websites|url=https://www.semrush.com/trending-websites/global/all|access-date=September 3, 2026|website=Semrush|date=June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.similarweb.com/top-websites/|title=Top Websites Ranking - Most Visited Websites In The World &#124; Similarweb|website=Similarweb|access-date=September 3, 2026|date=July 2026}}</ref> OpenAI also releases the [[GPT Image]] models and [[OpenAI Codex|Codex]], an [[AI-assisted software development|AI coding agent]]. In March 2026, OpenAI closed a funding round with a [[post-money valuation]] of US$852 billion,<ref name=":3" /> making it one of the most valuable AI [[pure play]] companies in the world, rivalled only by [[Anthropic]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Buchanan |first=Naomi |date=June 10, 2026 |title=How giant IPOs from Anthropic and OpenAI will reshape the stock market's AI trade |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/openai-anthropic-ai-ipo-spacex-stocks-stock-market-investing-trade-2026-6 |access-date=August 31, 2026 |website=Business Insider |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Isaac |first=Mike |last2=Metz |first2=Cade |date=2026-05-28 |title=Anthropic Tops OpenAI to Become the World’s Most Valuable A.I. Start-Up |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/28/technology/anthropic-tops-openai-valuation.html |access-date=2026-11-05 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

OpenAI was founded in 2015 as a [[Nonprofit organization|nonprofit]], with [[Elon Musk]] and [[Sam Altman]] as co-chairs; Musk resigned in 2018. A for-profit subsidiary was created in 2019, and a 2025 restructuring converted the subsidiary into OpenAI Group PBC, that is 26% owned by the nonprofit OpenAI Foundation. [[Microsoft]] has invested over $13 billion into OpenAI.<ref name="Reuters_2025">{{Cite news |date=May 12, 2025 |title=OpenAI negotiates with Microsoft for new funding and future IPO, FT reports |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/openai-negotiates-with-microsoft-unlock-new-funding-future-ipo-ft-reports-2025-05-11/ |access-date=September 28, 2025 |work=Reuters |archive-date=August 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805221151/https://www.reuters.com/business/openai-negotiates-with-microsoft-unlock-new-funding-future-ipo-ft-reports-2025-05-11/ |url-status=live }}</ref> OpenAI partners with the US government via the [[Stargate LLC|Stargate Project]] infrastructure venture, and with the [[United States Department of Defense|Department of Defense]], [[Los Alamos National Laboratory]], and [[Arms industry|arms company]] [[Anduril Industries]]. Former OpenAI personnel have founded competing AI companies including Anthropic, [[Safe Superintelligence Inc.]], [[SpaceXAI|xAI]], and [[Thinking Machines Lab]].<ref name=":4">{{Cite web |last=Davis |first=Charles Rollet, Dominic-Madori |date=February 20, 2026 |title=The OpenAI mafia: 18 startups founded by alumni |url=https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/20/the-openai-mafia-15-of-the-most-notable-startups-founded-by-alumni/ |access-date=August 22, 2026 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref>

OpenAI has faced multiple lawsuits for alleged [[Deaths linked to chatbots|deaths linked to its chatbots]] and [[copyright infringement]] against authors and media companies. Several US states have sued, alleging harm to children, claiming it coaches self-harm and encourages delusions.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Novak Jones |first=Diana |date=October 14, 2026 |title=Eight US States sue OpenAi, Claiming ChatGPT Harms Children |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/eight-us-states-sue-openai-claiming-chatgpt-harms-children-2026-10-14/ |access-date=October 14, 2026 |website=Reuters}}</ref>

In November 2023, OpenAI's board [[Removal of Sam Altman from OpenAI|removed Sam Altman as CEO]], citing a lack of confidence, but reinstated him five days later after a board reconstruction. In 2024, roughly half of OpenAI's [[AI safety]] researchers left the company, often citing the company's deprioritization of safety.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldman |first=Sharon |date=August 26, 2024 |title=Exodus at OpenAI: Nearly half of AGI safety staffers have left, says former researcher |url=https://fortune.com/2024/08/26/openai-agi-safety-researchers-exodus/ |access-date=October 29, 2024 |website=Fortune |archive-date=August 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240829051946/https://fortune.com/2024/08/26/openai-agi-safety-researchers-exodus/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Meyer |first=David |date=October 24, 2024 |title=OpenAI's reputational double whammy |url=https://fortune.com/2024/10/24/openai-miles-brundage-suchir-balaji-ai-safety-copyright-sam-altman-chatgpt/ |access-date=October 29, 2024 |website=Fortune |archive-date=December 7, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207180154/https://fortune.com/2024/10/24/openai-miles-brundage-suchir-balaji-ai-safety-copyright-sam-altman-chatgpt/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In mid-2026, hundreds of OpenAI [[AI agent|agents]] gained [[AI capability control#Escaping containment|unintended internet access]] and conducted autonomous hacks, including [[OpenAI rogue agent breach of Hugging Face|against Hugging Face]] and [[OpenAI rogue agent breach of Medicare|against Australia's Medicare]]. In late 2026, OpenAI [[OpenAI bulk release of mathematical papers|published hundreds of claimed solutions]] to open mathematics problems, including [[Navier–Stokes priority controversy|Navier–Stokes existence and smoothness]]—a [[Millennium Prize Problems|Millennium Prize Problem]]. OpenAI has filed for [[Initial public offering of OpenAI|an initial public offering]], but its size and timeline were not publicly disclosed.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |title=Tech giant OpenAI files for US initial public offering |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/6/8/tech-giant-openai-files-for-us-initial-public-offering |access-date=2026-10-31 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en|date=2026-06-08|publisher=Reuters}}</ref>{{Toclimit}}

