'''Renew Europe''' (or simply '''Renew''') is a [[Liberalism|liberal]], [[Centrism|centre]] to [[Centre-right politics|centre-right]], [[Pro-Europeanism|pro-European]] [[political group of the European Parliament]] founded for the [[ninth European Parliament]] term.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://alde.eu/en/news/1308-renew-europe/|title=Renew Europe. – News – ALDE|website=alde.eu|date=13 June 2019}}</ref> The group is the successor to the [[Alliance of Liberals and Democrats for Europe group|Alliance of Liberals and Democrats for Europe]] (ALDE) group which existed during the [[Sixth European Parliament|sixth]], [[Seventh European Parliament|seventh]] and [[Eighth European Parliament|eighth]] terms from 2004 to 2019, and under a variety of other names in earlier Parliaments.

The group announced the adoption of its new name on 12 June 2019, after forming an alliance with the French party [[La République En Marche!]], which wanted to avoid the word ''liberal'' in the name. The group continues to be known as the Liberal Group outside France.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.politico.eu/article/emmanuel-macron-liberal-alliance-to-be-named-renew-europe/|title=Macron-Liberal alliance to be named Renew Europe|last=Baume|first=Maïa de La|date=12 June 2019|website=Politico|access-date=12 June 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://euobserver.com/tickers/145134|title=[Ticker] Liberal Alde rename themselves 'Renew Europe'|website=EUobserver|date=12 June 2019}}</ref>

