'''SAP SE''' ({{IPAc-en|ˌ|ɛ|s|.|eɪ|ˈ|p|iː}}; {{IPA|de|ɛsʔaːˈpeː|-|De-SAP.ogg}}) is a German [[Multinational corporation|multinational]] software company based in [[Walldorf]], Baden-Württemberg, that is the world's largest vendor of [[enterprise software]].<ref>{{cite web |url= https://assets.cdn.sap.com/sapcom/docs/2017/04/4666ecdd-b67c-0010-82c7-eda71af511fa.pdf |title= SAP: The World's Largest Provider of Enterprise Application Software | publisher= SAP Global Communications |date= 28 April 2023 |access-date= 11 May 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= Reid |first= Jenni |date= 2025-03-25 |title= Software giant SAP becomes Europe's most valuable firm amid German stock market boom |url= https://www.cnbc.com/2025/03/25/sap-becomes-europes-most-valuable-firm-amid-german-stock-boom.html |access-date= 2025-04-25 |website= CNBC |language= en}}</ref> In June 2025, it was the largest European company by [[market capitalization]], as well as one of the 30 most valuable publicly traded companies in the world.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Companies ranked by Market Cap - CompaniesMarketCap.com |url=https://www.companiesmarketcap.com/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250626052126/https://www.companiesmarketcap.com/ |archive-date=2025-06-26 |access-date=2025-08-18 |website=www.companiesmarketcap.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

Founded in 1972 by five former IBM engineers, it now has offices in 78 countries<ref>{{Cite web |title=Worldwide Office Directory |url=https://www.sap.com/about/company/office-locations.html |website=SAP}}</ref> and 110,000 employees.<ref name="StockAnalysis_SAP_Mitarbeiter">{{cite web |url= https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sap/employes |title= SAP SE (SAP) Employees |website= StockAnalysis.com |publisher= Stock Analysis |access-date= 18 September 2026 |language= en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=SAP Company Information |url=https://www.sap.com/about/company.html |website=SAP}}</ref> It ranks in the top 10 of publicly traded software companies and is the largest in Europe.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Global 2000 2026 |url=https://www.forbes.com/lists/global2000/ |website=Forbes}}</ref>

SAP is a component of the [[DAX]] and [[Euro Stoxx 50]] stock market indices.<ref>{{cite web |title=Börse Frankfurt (Frankfurt Stock Exchange): Stock market quotes, charts and news |url=http://www.boerse-frankfurt.de/en/equities/indices/euro+stoxx+50+EU0009658145/constituents |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190208093448/http://www.boerse-frankfurt.de/en/equities/indices/euro%20stoxx%2050%20EU0009658145/constituents |archive-date=8 February 2019 |access-date=22 October 2015 |postscript=. As of 31 December 2024, SAP was the most valuable company in the DAX by market capitalization and was ranked among the top 5% in the S&P Global ESG Scores in the S&P Global Corporate Sustainability Assessment.}}</ref>

