The '''Spain national handball team''' is governed by the [[Royal Spanish Handball Federation]]. Spain is one of the most successful handball teams in the world, having won two [[IHF World Men's Handball Championship|World Championships]] and two [[European Men's Handball Championship|European Championships]]. They also have won medals in the three main international competitions: nine at [[European Men's Handball Championship|European Championships]], five at [[IHF World Men's Handball Championship|World Championships]] and five at [[Handball at the Summer Olympics|Olympic Games]] ([[Handball at the 1996 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|1996 Atlanta]], [[Handball at the 2000 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2000 Sydney]], [[Handball at the 2008 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2008 Beijing]], [[Handball at the 2020 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2020 Tokyo]] and [[Handball at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2024 Paris]]).

