'''World Rugby''' is the governing body for the sport of [[rugby union]].<ref name=times-1998/> World Rugby organises the [[Rugby World Cup]] every four years, the sport's most recognised and most profitable competition.<ref name="RWC Hist rfh">{{cite web|work=Rugby Football History |title=Rugby World Cup History |url=http://rugbyfootballhistory.com/world_cup.htm |access-date=14 July 2006 }}</ref> It also organises a number of other international competitions, such as the [[World Rugby Nations Cup (2026–)|Nations Cup]], the [[WXV Global Series]], the [[World Rugby Junior World Championship|Junior World Championship]], the [[Pacific Nations Cup]] and the [[SVNS]].

World Rugby's headquarters are in [[Dublin]], Ireland.<ref name=it-2014/><ref name=irb-org/> Its membership now comprises 133 national unions.<ref name="RW Handbook">{{cite web|url=https://www.worldrugby.org/member-unions|title=World Rugby Member Unions|work=World Rugby|access-date=17 April 2017}}</ref> Each member country must also be a member of one of the six regional unions into which the world is divided: Africa, North America, Asia, Europe, South America, and Oceania.{{sfn|World Rugby Handbook|2014|page=20}}

World Rugby was founded as the '''International Rugby Football Board''' ('''IRFB''') in 1886 by {{runion|Scotland}}, {{runion|Wales}} and {{runion|Ireland}}, with {{runion|England}} joining in 1890.{{sfn|IRB Handbook|2013|pages=15-20}} {{runion|Australia}}, {{runion|New Zealand}} and {{runion|South Africa}} became full members in 1949.{{sfn|IRB Handbook|2013|pages=15-20}} {{runion|France}} became a member in 1978 and a further 80 members joined from 1987 to 1999.{{sfn|IRB Handbook|2013|pages=15-20}} The body was renamed the '''International Rugby Board''' ('''IRB''') in 1998, and took up its current name of World Rugby in 2014.<ref name=irb-name-wr/> In 2009, the [[International Olympic Committee]] (IOC) voted to include rugby sevens in the [[2016 Summer Olympics]].<ref name=rfh-olmpics/> World Rugby gained membership of the [[Association of Summer Olympic International Federations]] (ASOIF) in 2010.<ref name=asoif>{{cite web |url=http://asoif.com/IFDirectory/ |title=Members |publisher=ASOIF |access-date=29 January 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150710081849/http://asoif.com/IFDirectory/ |archive-date=10 July 2015 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref>

