'''Yannick Agnel''' (born 9 June 1992) is a French former competitive [[Swimming (sport)|swimmer]] who specialized in [[freestyle swimming|freestyle]] events, and is a three-time [[Summer Olympic Games|Olympic]] [[Olympic medal|medalist]].  In his Olympic [[wiktionary:debut#Noun|debut]] at the [[2012 Summer Olympics]] in [[London]], he won gold in the [[Swimming at the 2012 Summer Olympics – Men's 200 metre freestyle|200-meter freestyle]], gold in the [[Swimming at the 2012 Summer Olympics – Men's 4 × 100 metre freestyle relay|4×100-meter freestyle relay]], and silver in the [[Swimming at the 2012 Summer Olympics – Men's 4 × 200 metre freestyle relay|4×200-meter freestyle relay]].  He is the current world record holder in the [[World record progression 400 metres freestyle|400-meter freestyle]] (short course) and the [[List of French records in swimming|national record]] holder in the 200- and 400-meter freestyle (long course).

Agnel's success earned him ''[[Swimming World Magazine|Swimming World]]''{{'s}} European Swimmer of the Year award in 2012.

